From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:27:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: require batched edit operations

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Require the edit tool batch operations input contract
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-fix
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1010-personal-fix-nudge-repeated-deterministic-tool-input-failures.patch
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 1011-personal-fix-require-batched-edit-operations.patch

Patch intent:
Require edit inputs to provide a non-empty edits array, remove top-level
single-edit shorthand, and retain the batch operation schema through the tested
OpenRouter and OpenAI strict schema mappings.

Why it exists:
The single-edit shorthand and batch form create inconsistent edit inputs and
schemas. Require the batch contract and reject malformed edit inputs before file
access, while preserving empty replacement strings for deletions.

Upstream integration points:
The change updates EditTool input parsing, validation, and parameters_schema in
crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/edit.rs. The file_diff and edit_stats tests use
the required edits array.

Update guidance:
Preserve the required non-empty edits array and reject only the three known
top-level shorthand fields. Keep empty new_string values valid so edits can
delete matched text. Avoid claims of OS-level write atomicity.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-app-core edit::tests --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core tool::file_diff --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core tool::edit_stats --lib
